import{I as s}from"./patterns-nav-bar-DO7t2iv4.js";import{I as r}from"./patterns-trace-BESFmCOG.js";import"./index-B0WjJBI_.js";import"./_commonjsHelpers-CqkleIqs.js";import"./index-x-G-dxfr.js";import"./index-CwPCC0ZT.js";const i=s.find(o=>o.name==="Pattern: Nav bar — Command"),g={title:"Examples/Nav bar/Nav bar — Command",component:r["Pattern: Nav bar — Command"],tags:["autodocs","needs-review"],parameters:{docs:{description:{component:'> ⚠️ **Needs review** — check these against Figma:\n>\n> - The kit\'s NavBar defaults to a "Home" stage; Figma now says "Command".\n\n**Figma:** Decisions — Default + Dev Notes [patterns] (244:119950)\n\n# Nav bar (stage navigation)\n\nPatterns file `KmmVU2D0kqWr0dC1xXNzWw`, page "Nav bar" 243:66369, section "nav bar" 244:119940.\n\n## What it is / when to use it\nThe Level-1 bar that switches between the product\'s stages, and what each stage brings with it. The page lays out one frame per stage under a sticky label: Command, Value, Explore, Build, Plan. Results, Search, Notification and User settings have labels but no frames. Use it as the top of every product screen. Each stage then supplies its own L2 sidebar (or none), header, content and bottom sheet.\n\n## Anatomy\n- `NavBar` (nav-bar-organism Type=Default): logo, stage tabs (`NavBarItem`), search / settings / notifications, avatar. Stages here: Command · Value · Explore · Build · Plan · Results. Pass them as `stages`; the kit default still says "Home".\n- `NavBarCollapsed` (Type=Collapsed / Collapsed opened): logo + hamburger (`IconButton` secondary S `system-hamburger-menu`) in the Pages slot. It opens a single-select list of the stages with a check on the current one.\n- `ResponsiveNavBar`: `NavBar` or `NavBarCollapsed`, chosen by width, with one shared stage value.\n- `StagedAppShell`: `AppShell` + `ResponsiveNavBar`, plus a `screens` map from stage to `{ sideNav, header, content, bottom }`.\n- L2 per stage, as the frames draw it:\n  - Command and Build: none.\n  - Value: `SideNav` (Active framework · LIBRARY: Strategy Framework / Value Frameworks / Value Models · Human Performance).\n  - Plan: `SideNavTree`, a folder tree plus an "Ad hoc plans" section with ＋.\n  - Explore: no sidebar. It has `ExploreHeader` under the bar.\n  - Plan and Explore also have a 48px collapsed right panel rail (sidebar-organism View=Collapsed).\n- Content:\n  - Command: `PageTop` (Cooper eyebrow, H1 greeting, description, `Tabs` with counts, `SmartSearch`), then "Decisions to review" + `SegmentedControl` S + display-settings `IconButton`. Below that, the ranked `HomeRowCard` list (first = Primary, rest = Secondary). A right column holds Cooper\'s results, the milestone (`ProgressBar`) and `Calendar`.\n  - Value / Build: `PageTop` (H1, description, "New" `Button`; no `PageHeader`), then `DataTable` (Value: standard, tabs + search outside the card; Build: `Tabs` L Idea Pad / Investments, ranked table with segmented filter).\n  - Explore: map with `MapPinDot` clusters, `MapToolbar` (top-left views, bottom-left default), `FtaButton`.\n  - Plan: title, description and owner. Then planning-cycle cards, the cycle\'s `StatCardsRow`, and an affected-area map (`MapPinPole`, `MapPinDot`).\n- Bottom: `BottomSheet` with two prompts. Command and Build: base. Value: base under the content column only. Plan: `type="value"` with Cooper\'s Context "16 Documents" + upload. Explore: none.\n\n## Flows and states\n1. **Stage switching.** Click a stage tab, or pick one from the hamburger list. The active tab gets the header-item active fill. The whole shell below the bar changes: sidebar, header, content and bottom sheet.\n2. **L2 selection.** Value: picking a sidebar row changes the page title and table. Plan: a tree row selects that plan and expands its folder; the caret toggles a folder without selecting it. The open path is outlined, and the current folder is also filled.\n3. **Sidebar collapse.** `arrow-bar-left` collapses the sidebar to a 48px rail; `arrow-bar-right` expands it.\n4. **Responsive.** ≥ 1280: full shell. Below 1280: sidebars start as rails. Below 800: the bar becomes `NavBarCollapsed`. (All three thresholds inferred; Figma only draws 1440 frames and a 600px Collapsed variant.)\n5. **Hamburger list.** Opens 4px under the button. Arrow keys / Home / End move, Enter picks, Esc or an outside click closes. Picking a stage closes the list.\n6. **Command list.** The tabs (My works / Decisions / Conversations / Following) change the list. The priority segmented control filters it; with nothing at that priority, an all-done `EmptyState` shows. Opening a decision goes to the stage on its badge (Explore / Build / Plan). (inferred)\n7. **HomeRowCard states.** Default, Hover (tertiary-alpha fill), Focus (ring), Loading (skeleton bars, no media, arrow disabled).\n\n## Rules\n- One L1 bar on every screen: 48px, sticky, full width, logo left, actions right, exactly one stage active. (Figma)\n- The stage order is fixed: Command, Value, Explore, Build, Plan, Results. (Figma)\n- When the tabs don\'t fit, collapse to the hamburger variant. Don\'t wrap or scroll the tabs. (Figma variant; trigger width inferred)\n- The L2 sidebar belongs to the stage. A stage with no sections has no sidebar (Command, Build) and gives the content the full width. (Figma frames)\n- On map stages (Explore), the explore-header sits directly under the bar instead of a page header. (Figma)\n- Only the top item of the Command list is Primary (gradient stroke, media). Every other item is Secondary. (Figma)\n- HomeRowCard metrics are CPV and V/C. Long titles and descriptions truncate on one line. (Figma; truncation inferred)\n- The bottom sheet\'s prompts are specific to the screen (e.g. "Why is Northgate #1?" on Command). (Figma)\n\n## Don\'ts\n- Don\'t mix `global-header` and `nav-bar-organism`: use `NavBar` / `NavBarCollapsed` everywhere.\n- Don\'t add a sidebar to a stage that has no sections.\n- Don\'t make more than one HomeRowCard Primary.\n- Don\'t put stage navigation in `Tabs`. Tabs are for peer views inside a page.\n\n## Consolidated / unsure\n- consolidated: `global-header` (8a567522…, Plan home 244:120469) → `NavBar` / nav-bar-organism. Same 48px bar, padding, gaps, fills, blur, stroke, items and actions. It differs only by legacy atoms (`header-item`, `avatar`, `Icon Button / Notification`), no slots, no collapsed variants, and an unused "Show recomendation" bool (nav-bar-organism has a hidden badge-atom in its place). nav-bar-organism is marked "use this".\n- consolidated: `Switcher` / `switcher container` (9087521b… / 609a3312…, not published in IFS DS) → `SegmentedControl size="s"`. Same 24px items, padding 0/8 and container padding 2. Text is H4/medium and the fills are surface tokens instead of element tokens.\n- consolidated: `segmented-control-icon` (882a35e9…, Patterns-local 244:119673) → `IconButton` (secondary) or `SegmentedControl` with icon options.\n- consolidated: `compare-quick-stat-card` (35bab075… = legacy stat-capital-flow-card) → `StatCard` in `StatCardsRow`.\n- consolidated: `tableHeader` / `tableCell` (609b40c3… / 81b10bef…) → `DataTable`.\n- consolidated: `Evidence-strip-bar/all actions` (4512b2ec…, Plan) → `BottomSheet type="value"` (Cooper\'s Context + documents + upload + prompts + FAB).\n- consolidated: `ai smart search` → `SmartSearch`.\n- `page-top` → `PageTop` (designer decision, Oct 2026). Command uses it with the Cooper eyebrow and no button; Value and Build use it as the page intro. Build\'s is a detached copy (title only, Tabs L).\n- **UNSURE: `explore-header` (ae9026ad…, used here) vs `explore-header-pattern` (0f49a18b…, IFS DS 7205:33581).** Same purpose. The one used here has no variants (search + filter left; collaborators + comments right), while the published set has show-cooper-badge / show-selected / show-action-buttons / show-back-button. Built as `ExploreHeader` from the instance used here.\n- **UNSURE: Plan sidebar tree.** Figma fills sidebar-organism\'s Content slot with detached `tableCell` frames (caret + folder + label, tree guide lines). There is no DS tree component. Built as the `SideNavTree` composite.\n- Not found on this page: `sidebar-value` (7d91409b…). The Value sidebar here is `sidebar-pattern` Page=Value = `SideNav`.\n'}},design:{type:"figma",url:"https://www.figma.com/design/KmmVU2D0kqWr0dC1xXNzWw/IFS-Design-System-Patterns?node-id=244-119950"}}},e={name:"All variants & states",render:()=>i.render()};var a,t,n;e.parameters={...e.parameters,docs:{...(a=e.parameters)==null?void 0:a.docs,source:{originalSource:`{
  name: 'All variants & states',
  render: () => section.render()
}`,...(n=(t=e.parameters)==null?void 0:t.docs)==null?void 0:n.source}}};const u=["AllVariants"];export{e as AllVariants,u as __namedExportsOrder,g as default};
